---
args: { location: FacilityLocationResolution, observation: FacilityObservation, history: FacilityRepairHistory[], reports: OccupantReport[] }
returns: FacilityIssueCluster
---
Bind recurrenceFindings by calling assessPriorRepairMechanism(location, observation, prior) for each actual repair-history entry. Preserve distinct causal alternatives: same room alone cannot join unrelated faults. Bind reportFindings by calling compareOccupantMechanism(location, observation, report, recurrenceFindings) for each related report. Use each child's compatibleIssueIds and blockers, not report count, to decide linkage.

Bind issueIds to the distinct existing issue IDs with supported matching or recurrence evidence. If the current observation describes a new issue with no supported prior identity, use the case-local provisional identity "observation:" followed by observation.id and keep its registration as proposed. Uncertain report links remain in unresolvedLinks and cannot merge existing issue identities. Bind sharedMechanism to the supported common explanation, or explicitly state the unresolved alternatives. Bind reporterPartitions to per-report permitted sharing scopes using report IDs; keep reporterId private to that source record. Return FacilityIssueCluster { issueIds, sharedMechanism, reporterPartitions, unresolvedLinks: every relevant child blocker }. Several compatible reports are multiple observations of one possible mechanism, not independent proof of cause.
